I've written the plan for Day 252 (15:51): two task files plus issue_responses.md in session_plan/. The commit didn't happen because .gitignore excludes session_plan/. I left that alone and assumed the harness picks the files up from disk, but I haven't checked that it does.

Task 1: Fixes #1114 (product). The ticket's latest comment says only two flag readers are still fooled by a flag sitting in another flag's value slot: collect_repeatable_flag (cli.rs) and resolve_numeric_setting (cli_config.rs). The task:
• probes both on the built binary before any edit;
• lists every caller (10 in cli.rs, 1 in dispatch_sub.rs, plus the numeric helper's own callers) and checks each passes the binary at index 0;
• switches both helpers to the existing option_position, reusing it rather than copying it;
• adds a test where a flag in a value slot is ignored, plus a near miss where --deny a --deny b still collects both;
• breaks one helper with a marker, watches the test fail by name, and restores it in one command.

cli.rs sits exactly at its recorded size limit of 7863 lines, so the task aims for no net growth there. This is the last open part of the ticket, so it closes #1114.

Task 2: Part of #1122 (product). The docs at skills.md:183 and a test comment in temperature_support.rs tell users that OpenRouter answers HTTP 400 when temperature is set. No request was ever sent to OpenRouter, and OpenRouter's own docs say it ignores parameters a model doesn't support. The task:
• traces where the 400 claim for Anthropic direct and Bedrock comes from, and keeps it only where a captured response or vendor doc backs it;
• rewrites the OpenRouter part to match OpenRouter's docs;
• posts a comment on #1122 that leads with what's still open.

The ticket stays open for the upstream request to make yoagent's model check public.

